# Thesis Experiment and Writing Plan
# RAG vs Fine-Tuning vs Hybrid for repository-level code completion
# Data: CrossCodeEval + RepoBench (no raw repo data required)

===========================================================================
## 0. GOAL AND DECISION QUESTION
===========================================================================
Compare RAG-only (System A), fine-tuning-only (System B), and hybrid (System C)
under identical conditions: same base model (Qwen2.5-Coder-1.5B), same prompts,
same metrics, same repository knowledge, no test-target leakage.

Decision question (use as the thesis objective):
  Given a private repository and a single-GPU budget, which adaptation strategy
  should a team choose, and when does the hybrid's extra complexity pay off?

Application domain (for the thesis and defense):
  Developer tooling for software companies working on private codebases.
  Privacy constraints often prevent sending proprietary code to commercial
  APIs, so teams self-host small open models and must choose how to adapt them
  under limited GPU budgets.

